4. Speech Generation — IMPORTANT ARCHITECTURE CHANGE

Previously, the project used:

Fish Audio for text-to-speech.
Chatterbox in an older implementation.
Faster-Whisper for speech recognition.

We decided to REMOVE Fish Audio, Chatterbox, and Faster-Whisper completely from the final architecture.

The intended architecture is:

Qwen3-ASR-1.7B: speech recognition.
Qwen3.8:27B: conversational intelligence.
A replacement natural-sounding TTS engine: speech generation.
LiveKit: real-time voice communication.

The replacement TTS engine has NOT yet been selected and integrated.

The priority is finding a high-quality natural English voice that works on the available ARM64 Linux environment.

Do not assume a particular TTS engine is already installed.

Investigate compatibility before recommending installation.

